---
// UNUSED since 2026-10-02. Superseded by the nine-chapter home in
// src/components/home/; nothing under src/pages/ imports it, directly or
// transitively. Kept rather than deleted in the same change that replaced it,
// so the old page can still be read while the new one settles.
//
// Delete on or after 2026-11-02 if it is still unreferenced. Verify first —
// `grep -rl <name> src/` from apps/site — rather than trusting this header.
// apps/site/src/components/SiteNav.astro
//
// No version badge. It read the CLI's version at build time, but the site only
// deploys on its own site-v* tag, so every CLI release left it stale — it said
// v2.0.0 while npm served 2.0.1. Fixing it by deploying the site on CLI tags
// would let a patch release publish unreleased site content; see Plan 15 task 5.
// There is one laqi and the install command names no version, so the badge had
// nothing to tell a visitor that the page does not already say.
---
<header class="site-nav">
  <a href="/" class="brand">
    <img src="/icon.svg" alt="" width="15" height="20" />
    <span>laqi</span>
  </a>
  <nav>
    <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
    <a href="/docs/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
    <a href="/docs/concepts/resolution-layers/">Concepts</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/csdev19/laqi/tree/main/examples">Examples</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/csdev19/laqi">GitHub</a>
  </nav>
  <a href="/docs/" class="search">Search docs <kbd>⌘K</kbd></a>
</header>

<style>
  .site-nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .brand {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-left: 1rem;
  }
  nav a {
    color: var(--dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  nav a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .search {
    margin-left: auto;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--bd);
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--dim);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
